{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15410876","formula":"C₁₀H₈O₈S₂","hill":"C10H8O8S2","elements":["H","C","O","S"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":8.0,"O":8.0,"S":2.0},"names":{"en":"Chromotropic acid","ru":"Хромотроповая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chromotropic acid is an organic compound with the chemical formula (HO)2C10H4(SO3H)2. Its name is derived from the two ancient Greek words χρωμός (chromos, color) and τροπέιν or τρέπω (verb: tropein, trepo, changing, turning), meaning it changes of color when reacting with some other compounds. This property is put to use in analytical chemistry for the colorimetric assay of various compounds such as formaldehyde, nitrate anions and even some herbicides.","ru":"Хромотро́повая кислота (4,5-дигидрокси-2,7-нафталиндисульфоновая кислота) — органическое химическое вещество, относящееся к классам сульфокислот и фенолов. Динатриевая соль хромотроповой кислоты (также называемая «хромотроп»), обычно поставляемая в виде дигидрата — реагент в аналитической химии."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":67221,"mass":320.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=C2C=C(C=C(C2=C(C=C1S(=O)(=O)O)O)O)S(=O)(=O)O","inchikey":"HLVXFWDLRHCZEI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4,5-dihydroxynaphthalene-2,7-disulfonic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"67221","atoms":28,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.944,"y":-1.152,"z":0.085,"el":"S"},{"x":3.944,"y":-1.151,"z":-0.085,"el":"S"},{"x":1.306,"y":3.175,"z":-0.028,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.306,"y":3.175,"z":0.028,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.349,"y":-1.366,"z":-1.485,"el":"O"},{"x":4.35,"y":-1.366,"z":1.484,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.689,"y":-2.472,"z":0.641,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.93,"y":-0.27,"z":0.689,"el":"O"},{"x":3.689,"y":-2.472,"z":-0.641,"el":"O"},{"x":4.93,"y":-0.269,"z":-0.69,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":-0.291,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.125,"z